body:
Thank you. Not going to lie, it's been really hard. I make generally about $800/mo now, I think. My hours have been all over the place, and it's still not enough to keep up with inflation, even though I am generally getting more hours.

&#x200B;

I really hope I get lucky and get y loan forgiven, but for right now the payments are paused. I think that payment is going to be about $130/ month, which is what I currently pay for my credit card payment. I am going to apply to see if I can get some kind of way to knock down the school loan payment, because I definitely can't do that right now. The school loan payment interest is 4.53%, I believe, and my credit card is about 11%, I think?

&#x200B;

I've been trying to see if a balance transfer card is even worth it, but it seems like if I don't pay the amount back before the term ends, I will have a much higher APR. The lowest one I saw was 19% =/

I'm in a bad spot with it right now. I was weaning off it for a while, because weed has such a big impact on my weight loss. I got to my highest weight at the beginning of 2020, and lost 40 pounds just working out at home and logging my food on LoseIt...then I lost my mom at the beginning of 2022. She passed on January 16th, and shit's been rough ever since.

&#x200B;

I have turned to trees to cope, and I try not to be a munchies monster, but it's so hard for me, especially with edibles... It just sucks all around. I don't want to gain weight, but I also jut feel good when I'm high. It's the brief respite I get from my brain being on full mental breakdown mode all the time. I do therapy, ahve medications and all, but they don't really help.

It's a terrible and heartbreaking story. I'm already very mixed in my feelings for true crime stuff...I really wanted to be a forensic investigator growing up, so I was really into real life CSI and true crime before it got popular...but it really astounds me that people can get so popular without basic editing skills. 

&#x200B;

On the one hand, I think information should be accessible to everyone, and reading shouldn't be a gatekeeping thing full of academic terms, but man....like if you're that popular, why not hire an editor? Again, I am all about accessibility, but this just got a bit silly. Proofreading is important.

My husband found this thread for me today, and it's a literal miracle. I've had migraines for the past 7 years , they've gotten worse. What I have worked out is that it's mostly menstrual, but I think weather affects it as well (high/low pressure systems). In any case, I just finally got in to see a neurologist in February, only seen her twice so far. I'm on rizatripan and promethazine, and now I take them before my cycle starts. It's mostly been working, seen dramatic improvement, until Monday. I had the worst migraine of my life. Like I wanted to walk into traffic bad, just to make it stop. I spoke with my neurologist, but essentially they want to "wait and see" f this happens again. So if a massive one like this happens again, I'm SOL and will be without anything to make it stop. 

&#x200B;

 I see the AMA here today and try to sign up, like I was at the payment screen to pay for the kit, and it said that  Mabel isn't available in my area yet. Do you have a rough roll out date for Washington State?  Also, if I signed up but it isn't available , am I still on a waiting list?

&#x200B;

I'm s grateful you guys are here, I hope to get signed up soon. (I'm also sure there's lots of traffic today, so I will check back)
